M/s Sunrise Publishers
Daryaganj, New Delhi – 110002

Subject: Complaint regarding damaged consignment of Class 10 books (Order No. KV/412)

Sir/Madam,

With reference to our order no. KV/412 dated 10 November 2026 for 60 Class 10 Science and Mathematics reference sets, the consignment arrived yesterday. Upon inspection, 15 volumes had torn spines, water-stained pages, and missing chapter indices due to damp packaging.

Since annual board preparation is underway, kindly arrange free replacement of these 15 defective copies within seven working days, failing which we shall have to adjust the invoice accordingly.

Yours faithfully,
Priya
(School Librarian)', 'Formal business letter format [1 Mark] | Order reference + defect details + resolution timeline [2 Marks] | Coherence & polite firm tone [1 Mark] | Accuracy [1 Mark]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Always invent a clean Order Number and specific quantity of defective items. | Common Pitfall: Missing invoice/order reference date or writing rude language.', 'HARD', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c1', 'Study the comparative reading preference data among teenagers between 2020 and 2025:
Printed Fiction: 42% (2020) -> 30% (2025); E-Books: 28% (2020) -> 38% (2025); Audiobooks: 10% (2020) -> 20% (2025); Newspapers/Magazines: 20% (2020) -> 12% (2025). Write an analytical paragraph in 100–120 words.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'English', 'Writing', 5, 'The comparative data highlights a decisive digital transition in teenage reading habits between 2020 and 2025. While printed fiction was the top preference in 2020 at 42%, it declined sharply by 12 percentage points to 30% in 2025. Similarly, print newspapers and magazines experienced a drop from 20% to 12%. In stark contrast, digital formats surged: e-books climbed from 28% to overtake print as the leading medium at 38%, while audiobooks doubled from 10% to 20%. Overall, screen and audio formats combined rose from 38% to 58% over five years, reflecting teens'' preference for portable, on-the-go reading convenience.', 'Clear trend overview (print decline vs digital rise) [1 Mark] | Exact comparisons (42%->30%, 28%->38%, 10%->20%) [2 Marks] | Comparative vocabulary (sharp contrast, doubled) [1 Mark] | Accuracy [1 Mark]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Highlight both highest growth (audiobooks doubled) and crossover point (e-books overtaking print). | Common Pitfall: Listing raw numbers without comparison words like "declined", "doubled", or "overtook".', 'HARD', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c2', 'Read the thematic context and answer:
During his historic 1994 inauguration as South Africa''s first Black President, Nelson Mandela spoke of "an extraordinary human disaster that lasted too long" and declared that "the oppressor must be liberated just as surely as the oppressed."

Answer the questions (5 Marks):
(a) What "extraordinary human disaster" does Mandela refer to? (1M)
(b) Why does Mandela believe the oppressor is also a prisoner who needs liberation? (2M)
(c) Name the twin obligations Mandela says every individual has in life. (2M)', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'English', 'Literature Extract (Prose)', 5, '(a) The brutal system of racial discrimination called Apartheid in South Africa.
(b) Mandela explains that a person who takes away another''s freedom is a prisoner of hatred, locked behind bars of prejudice and narrow-mindedness; both robbed and robber lose humanity.
(c) 1. Obligation to one''s family, parents, spouse, and children.
2. Obligation to one''s people, community, and country.', '(a) Apartheid / racial discrimination [1 Mark] | (b) Prisoner of hatred & prejudice [2 Marks] | (c) Twin obligations: family & nation/community [2 Marks]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Quote the key NCERT phrase: "prisoner of hatred, locked behind the bars of prejudice and narrow-mindedness". | Common Pitfall: Describing only the oppressed suffering without explaining the oppressor''s captivity.', 'HARD', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c3', 'Describe two comical arguments between Lomov and Natalya that interrupt Lomov''s marriage proposal. (40–50 words)', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'English', 'First Flight', 3, 'First, they quarrel fiercely over ownership of the small patch of land "Oxen Meadows" until Lomov suffers palpitations. Later, after reconciliation, they argue bitterly again over whose hunting dog—Guess or Squeezer—is superior.', 'Core textual point & reasoning (2M) + Expression (1M) [3 Marks]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Keep exact names: Oxen Meadows, Guess (Lomov''s dog), Squeezer (Natalya''s dog). | Common Pitfall: Exceeding 50 words or missing exact character names.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c4', 'What caused Matilda Loisel''s ten years of gruelling poverty, and what ironic truth awaited her at the end? (40–50 words)', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'English', 'Footprints Without Feet', 3, 'Matilda borrowed a diamond necklace from Madame Forestier for a ball and lost it. Too proud to confess, the Loisels borrowed 36,000 francs to buy a replacement and laboured a decade to repay the debt—only to learn later that the original necklace was false paste worth under 500 francs!', 'Core textual point & reasoning (2M) + Expression (1M) [3 Marks]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Cite exact figures: 36,000 francs vs 500 francs. | Common Pitfall: Giving vague moral statements without textual incidents.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c5', '[Read Passage: "Solar Microgrids Transforming Remote Himalayan Hamlets"]
Perched above 3,800 metres in Ladakh and Spiti, remote mountain villages once remained disconnected from national power grids due to steep terrain and heavy winter snowfall that snapped overhead cables. Today, decentralised DC solar microgrids have brought clean electricity to over 200 high-altitude hamlets. Powered by high-efficiency photovoltaic panels that perform strongly in crisp mountain sunlight, each microgrid feeds lithium-ferro-phosphate battery banks housed in insulated rooms. Reliable evening lighting has extended study hours for school students, replaced smoky kerosene lamps, and powered solar water pumps for greenhouse vegetable cultivation.

Why could conventional overhead grid lines not serve high-altitude Himalayan villages reliably?', '{"A":"Lack of sunlight in Ladakh","B":"Steep terrain and heavy winter snowfall snapping cables","C":"Absence of batteries","D":"Excess humidity"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Reading Comprehension', 1, 'Option (B) is correct. Steep terrain and heavy winter snow snapped conventional overhead power cables.', 'Correct option (B) from passage evidence [1 Mark]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Locate the exact phrase in the passage before selecting. | Common Pitfall: Relying on outside knowledge rather than passage facts.', 'EASY', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c6', '[From Passage "Solar Microgrids Transforming Remote Himalayan Hamlets"] Where are the battery banks stored to survive sub-zero Himalayan winters?', '{"A":"Open rooftops","B":"Insulated rooms","C":"Riverbeds","D":"Wooden poles"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Reading Comprehension', 1, 'Option (B) is correct. Battery banks are housed in insulated rooms.', 'Correct option (B) from passage evidence [1 Mark]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Locate the exact phrase in the passage before selecting. | Common Pitfall: Relying on outside knowledge rather than passage facts.', 'EASY', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c7', '[From Passage "Solar Microgrids Transforming Remote Himalayan Hamlets"] How has solar microgrid lighting directly benefited school students in these hamlets?', '{"A":"Reduced school terms","B":"Extended reliable evening study hours without smoky kerosene lamps","C":"Replaced textbooks with TV","D":"Closed village libraries"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Reading Comprehension', 1, 'Option (B) is correct. Clean evening light replaced smoky kerosene lamps and extended study hours.', 'Correct option (B) from passage evidence [1 Mark]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Locate the exact phrase in the passage before selecting. | Common Pitfall: Relying on outside knowledge rather than passage facts.', 'EASY', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c8', '[From Passage "Solar Microgrids Transforming Remote Himalayan Hamlets"] Besides lighting, microgrids support food security in cold deserts by:', '{"A":"Running coal furnaces","B":"Powering solar water pumps for greenhouse vegetable cultivation","C":"Importing tropical fruits","D":"Melting glaciers artificially"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Reading Comprehension', 1, 'Option (B) is correct. Microgrids power solar water pumps for greenhouse vegetable farming.', 'Correct option (B) from passage evidence [1 Mark]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Locate the exact phrase in the passage before selecting. | Common Pitfall: Relying on outside knowledge rather than passage facts.', 'EASY', true)
