Subject: Enquiry regarding 4-week Winter Python & Robotics Bootcamp

Sir/Madam,

I am a Class 10 student keen to enrol in your upcoming 4-week Python and Robotics Bootcamp advertised in yesterday''s local daily. Before registering, I would appreciate specific details regarding:
1. Batch timings and weekend schedule
2. Total fee structure and early-bird concessions
3. Whether Arduino/sensor hardware kits are included for hands-on practice
4. Availability of project-completion certificates

Kindly share the brochure and admission form via email or post at your earliest convenience.

Yours sincerely,
Kabir', 'Format completeness [1 Mark] | All 4 enquiry points covered concisely [2 Marks] | Logical bullet organisation [1 Mark] | Grammar & spelling [1 Mark]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Numbering 3–4 enquiry points makes the letter crisp and examiner-friendly. | Common Pitfall: Forgetting to request fee or batch timing details.', 'HARD', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000cf', 'Read the context and answer:
In Robin Klein''s poem "Amanda!", a young girl escapes constant parental nagging about posture, homework, chocolate, and tidiness by imagining herself as a tranquil mermaid, an orphan roaming bare streets, and Rapunzel in a quiet tower.

Answer the questions (5 Marks):
(a) Why are Amanda''s thoughts enclosed in parentheses (brackets) across alternate stanzas? (2M)
(b) Why does Amanda wish to be an orphan or Rapunzel? (2M)
(c) What message does the poet convey to parents through this poem? (1M)', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'English', 'Literature Extract (Poetry)', 5, '(a) The brackets visually separate Amanda''s silent, imaginative inner escape from the sharp outward commands of her parent, showing she cannot speak back openly.
(b) To Amanda, being an orphan or Rapunzel represents complete freedom, silence, and peace away from relentless instructions and scolding.
(c) Children need respectful space, empathy, and balanced guidance rather than suffocating micromanagement.', '(a) Inner silent escapism vs outward scolding [2 Marks] | (b) Yearning for freedom & peace [2 Marks] | (c) Need for balanced parenting/freedom [1 Mark]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Note the irony: Amanda wants to be Rapunzel yet refuses to ever let her hair down! | Common Pitfall: Thinking Amanda genuinely dislikes her mother out of cruelty rather than craving breathing space.', 'HARD', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000d0', 'How can one still identify a traditional Goan baker ("pader") even today, and why was bread integral to Goan life? (40–50 words)', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'English', 'First Flight', 3, 'One can identify the pader by his bamboo staff jhang-jhang sound in the morning and traditional knee-length "kabai" dress. Breads like sweet bol, bolinhas, and sandwiches were essential for marriages, engagements, and Christmas feasts.', 'Core textual point & reasoning (2M) + Expression (1M) [3 Marks]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Use specific terms: pader, kabai, bol, bolinhas. | Common Pitfall: Exceeding 50 words or missing exact character names.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('10041111-0000-4000-8000-0000000000d1', 'How did education transform shy, stammering "Bholi" into confident "Sulekha" at her wedding? (40–50 words)', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'English', 'Footprints Without Feet', 3, 'Her compassionate village schoolteacher patiently encouraged Sulekha, removing her fear and stammer. Armed with self-respect and education, Sulekha later stood up boldly at the wedding mandap, refusing to marry greedy Bishamber Nath who demanded ₹5,000 dowry after seeing her pockmarks.', 'Core textual point & reasoning (2M) + Expression (1M) [3 Marks]', NULL, 'Examiner Tip: Contrast her childhood nickname Bholi with her real name Sulekha at the climax. | Common Pitfall: Giving vague moral statements without textual incidents.', 'MEDIUM', true)
